<p class="clause" id="section-1-1"><strong>1.1 Access and Use.</strong> Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, Provider hereby grants Client, and its Administrative Users (as defined below, individually, each a “<strong>User</strong>”), a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable right to access and use the hosted software-as-a-service offering described in the applicable Order Form (as defined below), during the Term, solely for use by the Users for Client’s internal business purposes (subject to Section 2.1(c)) in accordance with the terms and conditions herein (collectively, the “<strong>Services</strong>”). “<strong>Order Form</strong>” means (a) the Marketplace offer (including any public or private offer) together with the pricing dimensions, usage limits, and other terms selected by Client in that offer, (b) any online checkout accepted by Provider, or (c) other ordering document that references this Agreement and is signed by both Parties. Each Order Form will specify the Aixle offering(s) subscribed for and the applicable term, Fees, and usage limits. “<strong>Administrative Users</strong>” means Client’s employees and individual independent contractors (including personnel of Client’s managed service or cloud operations providers) whom Client authorizes to access or use the Services solely on Client’s behalf, subject to any seat or user limits in the applicable Order Form. Client shall be liable for all acts and omissions of Administrative Users and of any other individual who interacts with the Services on Client’s behalf (including individuals who approve, reject, or respond to workflow steps through Client’s collaboration tools, such as Slack or Microsoft Teams) as if Client performed such acts and omissions itself. Each User is responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of their login credentials and account details (whether login/password, authentication app, emailed code, or other means of verifying a